Subject: Reland "[parser] Only classify arrow parameters and set initializers
 in arrow heads"

This is a reland of commit d149767fe05516886351a46d4b573073187bfece.

Resolved the duplicate `CanBeArrowParameterDeclaration()` declaration in
`ExpressionScope` that resulted from auto-merging on top of
https://crrev.com/c/8537630.

Original change's description:
> [parser] Only classify arrow parameters and set initializers in arrow heads
>
> `VariableProxy` initializer positions in
> `ExpressionParsingScope::variable_list_` are only consumed by
> `ArrowHeadParsingScope::ValidateAndCreateScope`.
>
> Previously:
> - `ExpressionScope::SetInitializers` checked `CanBeExpression()` instead
>   of `CanBeArrowParameterDeclaration()`, so every comma expression and
>   every normal function call argument walked `variable_list_` in the
>   enclosing `ExpressionParsingScope`.
> - `ExpressionParsingScope::SetInitializers` returned `len - 1` instead
>   of `len`, causing subsequent calls to re-check the last initialized
>   variable.
> - `ParseExpressionCoverGrammar` and `ParseArguments` called
>   `ClassifyArrowParameter` and `SetInitializers` even when not parsing a
>   potential arrow head.
>
> Restrict `ClassifyArrowParameter` and `SetInitializers` to arrow head
> scopes and return `len` from `SetInitializers`.
>
